# Retrieval evaluation cases. One JSON object per line.
# Ground truth = owner (user) + document file name + a fragment the relevant chunk contains, so it survives re-chunking.
# "chunkHint" is only a hint for humans (0-based position at the time of writing); a fragment always wins over it.
# expectedSources: [] means the corpus has no answer; the question must not bring up anything from the asker's documents.
# semantic-only: the question shares (almost) no word with the answer, so only vector search can find it.
# Tags: paraphrase | semantic-only | exact-term | error-code | file-reference | split-info | ambiguous | multi-document | no-answer | isolation
